<div style="padding:10px;"><h1>History of Ayya Vaikundar</h1></div>
<div class="space"></div>
<div class="right"><a href="detail-history-of-ayya-vaikundar-in-tamil.aspx"> தமிழில் வாசிக்க</a></div>
<div class="space"></div>
<div style="padding:5px;">
<b><center style="font-size:25px;color:Maroon;">AYYA THUNAI</center></b>
<br />
<b><center style="font-size:18px;color:#0000ee;">HISTORY OF LORD NARAYANA’S INCARNATE LORD VAIKUNDAR</center></b>
<br /><br />
<center><img src="Images/thamarai.png" /></center>
<br /><br />
<center>‘Lord Narayana himself incarnated as Vaikundar’</center>
<br /><br />
<center><img src="Images/vaikudar.png" /></center>
<br /><br />
<b><center style="font-size:16px;color:Maroon;">SOURCE: AKILATHIRATTU</center></b>
<br /><br />
<span style="font-size:16px;color:Maroon;">Lord Vaikunda Swamy (C.1833 – C.1851):</span> According to the sacred book Akilathirattu which is comparable to the texts of Vedas, Lord Maha Vishnu, the creator and protector of the Universe, after ending Lord Krishna Avatar (incarnation), again himself incarnated as Lord Vaikundar which was the tenth manifestation in Kali Yuga as prophesied by Veda Vyasa in Adi Agama (Vedas).  While Veda agama Akilathirattu, reverently mentioned him as <b>Shri Pandaram, Aandavar, Shri Mayon, Shri Narayana, Lord Vishnu, Lord Thirumal, Shri Perumal, Ayya Narayana, Shri Sivanarayana and Shri Suryanarayana,</b> the devotees reverently worship him in the names of <b>‘Ayya’, ‘Lord Vaikunda Swami’ and ‘Lord Narayana Swami’</b>.
<br /><br />
The divine philosophy has been that whenever Adharma raised its ugly head, and threatened to destroy basic fabrics of Dharma, God, mainly Lord Maha Vishnu incarnated in some form of human and destroyed Adharma to re-establish the rule of Dharma. True to this philosophy, Lord Maha Vishnu’s incarnation as Lord Vaikundar in Kaliyuga, was meant to end the suffering and humiliation of mankind by destroying evil Kali and re-establish rule of law called Dharma. The glories of Lord Vaikundar, who incarnated to destroy evil Kali has been elegantly eulogized in the form of verses in Tamil in the sacred religious scripture Holy Akilathirattu, which contain the divine acts and doctrines of Lord Vaikundar as penned by Shri Arigopalan Citar. The sacred Akilathirattu is considered to be one of the sacred Veda Agama texts, similar to the ancient Veda texts written by Maharishi Veda Vyasa. It has been written as verses in the form of poem consisting of more than 15000 words. The original Akilathirattu has been reportedly recorded on palm leaves until it was printed in book form. The entire contents according to him have been penned by him as dictated by Lord Vaikundar in his dream on the 27th day of the Tamil Month Karthigai in the year Kollam which was 1016, corresponding to Friday, the 10th December 1841 CE. The place where this sacred text has been written by Shri Arigopalan Citar is called ‘Thenthamaraikulam Pathi’ 
<br /><br />
The Holy Akilathirattu narrates the origin and evolution of the universe, time line of the evolutionary history covering major events, and subsequent developments which shaped our land over billions of years, after the cosmic had been created. Holy Akilathirattu explains various incarnations of Lord Maha Vishnu who finally incarnated in Kaliyuga as Lord Vaikundar and prophecy for the future.
<br /><br />
