<br /><br />
<span style="font-size:16px;color:Maroon;">Past Incarnations of Lord Mahavishnu:</span> According to the Veda agama Akilathirattu, God who is omnipresent and pervades in the universe is one and the same though they may appear in different forms such as Lord Shiva, Goddess Shakthi, Lord Omkara, Lord Vishnu, Lord Rudra, and Lord Maheshwar etc.  Prime divine during creation of the Cosmic, reportedly created 8.4 more million of active and inactive souls of different nature after which he created Deva Ganas, Asura Ganas serving in Deva Loga, Vedic sastras, Lord Sun and Lord Vayu to establish the concept of Dharma. 
<br /><br />
Once the cosmic embodied with cycles of Yugas and varieties of creatures were created, Lord Adi Brahma, named the first Yuga as ‘Neettiya Yuga’. A fire ritual (Agni Kund meant for performing Yagna and Homa) was performed by Lord Shiva to incorporate appropriate aspects for the universe, in which, host of divine forces besides Lord Vishnu and Lord Brahma participated to discuss the fabric of attributes and aspects to be incorporated in the universe. As the discussion continued, an evil asura called ‘Kroni’, emerged from the Agni Kund and within days of his appearance, he began terrorising the Celestial forces, destroyed the divine abodes and even attempted to destroy mount Kailash. Realizing the danger posed by the acts of the asura, Lord Maha Vishnu sat in penance seeking powers from Lord Shiva to annihilate Asura Kroni and to save the divine abodes and the Celestials. Lord Shiva while granting the boons, instructed Lord Maha Vishnu to kill Kroni by cutting him into six pieces, further indicating that all the six pieces of fleshes would again get birth in some form of an Asura or Monster in the Yugas to follow, and therefore Lord Maha Vishnu too would have to incarnate repeatedly in different forms to annihilate the Asuras born out of the flesh of evil Kroni in course of time in each of the Yugas.   
<br /><br />
