<br /><br />
Lord Maha Vishnu named the seven male kids as Sanar, Sandroars, and Nadalvar. Further he anointed them with 13 more such names, left them under the custody of Goddess Bhadra Kali, and proceeded to Srirangam where he rested in full purview of the universe. Mother Bhadra Kali, natured those boys very well, and imparted master arts and skills of several in nature, and thereafter took their help to annihilate Thakkan. Subsequently she got them married to the seven maidens, daughters of King Nriputharajan and settled them in seven separate houses specially built for them, where they lived with all comforts and glory.     
<br /><br />
During the same period of time, in Deva Loga, Guru Muni (Sage), along with the Celestials went to Lord Shiva and reminded him that appropriate time to bring out the Kali Yuga in the universe had already arisen. Acceding to the request of the Sage and the Celestials, Lord Shiva converted the last and sixth flesh of slayed Kroni into an asura named Kalian representing Kaliyuga who in fact was Duryodhana in his previous birth. Lord Shiva bestowed several boons to Kalian. He transformed one of the bones of Kalian, taken out from his hip into a female embodied with half the strength of Kalian and got Kalian married to her.  Henceforth Kalian will be referred as Kalineesan or evil Kali too. After obtaining several boons from Lord Shiva, as Kalian was returning to his place, Lord Maha Vishnu in disguise of a Pandaram (mendicant), wearing torn clothes, uncouth in appearance with braided hairs, blocked his way demanding that he part away some of the boons he received, lest he would not allow Kalian to continue the journey unless he defeated him (Lord Maha Vishnu in disguise of Pandaram) in a fight.  Kalian shied away to fight with him saying that even women would laugh if he chose to fight a Pandaram like him who had no weapons in hand to fight.  On insistence from Lord Maha Vishnu, to fight or part with the boons, Kalian promised on oath that he (Kalian) would never ever harm any Pandaram or mendicant, and if any Pandaram or mendicant was harmed by him (Kalian), the entire boons possessed by him would be lost.
<br /><br />
Dear devotees, only to snatch away the powerful boons in possession of Kalian alias Kalineesan, Lord Maha Vishnu appeared in guise of a Pandaram and met Kalineesan in the name of ‘Shri Pandaram’ so mention Holy Akilathirattu in beautiful tamil ‘yeraniyum maayon ivvulagil thavasu panni kaaranam pola seitha kathai’ meaning the story of the most beautiful and elegant Lord Maha Vishnu who undertook a unique penance for specific reason. 
<br /><br />
Once Kalineesan descended on earth, the entire atmosphere turned from good to worse. The evil forces unleashed intolerance, impiety, wickedness, unrighteousness and impudence all over the universe. The folks began ignoring the doctrines of sacred Vedas. Good animals, birds and other living creatures deserted the main land and went to the forest in search of Lord Mahavishnu, who appeared before them in the form of a Mendicant (Pandaram in Tamil) and advised them to stay in penance seeking incarnation of Lord Mahavishnu to re-establish kingdom of righteousness (Dharma) and take over the reins of the state. On the strength of the boons, Kalineesan spread hatred amongst people of different castes, kept them divided into many castes, created fiction to rebel against each other for their own selfish interests.  Burdening the folks with heavier taxes, he not even spared the sacred Mangal sutra (Wedding badge or string or thick yellow thread with a symbol knotted in the neck of bride) or dry leaves falling from the trees from the purview of taxation. 
<br /><br />
Cows were made` to starve.  When canon of justice and righteousness in the universe began to get destroyed, folks remained divided over caste lines, ethics, moral and human values dwindled to their low ebb in Kali Yuga. In view of the atrocities committed by Kalian, nature’s fury caused heavy downpour and torrential rainfall which lashed the state inundating many areas. Further the walls of huge Vaigai river burst and water began entering into the cities. The Chola King Kari Kalan immediately summoned the Sandroars and ordered that the breach be sealed with mud and sand brought in the baskets, ignoring the fact that the Sandroars too were also Kings of his stature. When they refused to carry out his order, he got two of them trampled to death under the feet of an elephant. When Lord Narayana heard of it from Saint Vidyathara, he immediately came there in the name of Chokkar, himself carried mud in a basket for pudding (called puttu in tamil given as alms for services) in between taking lashes from the guards, but ultimately ensuring that the life of remaining five Sandroars were saved. He then went to Srirangam in fit of rage and took rest there. 
<br /><br />
Rogues and criminals exploited the people. Thefts, fear and slovenes increased, gambling and corruption were rampant and murders and killings became order of the day. Sacred texts of ethics and morals (Shastra) tweaked and concocted to suit the rulers resulting in the folks adapting wrong rituals and practices. Maladies of mind and body increased and morality reached the lowest ebb. Folks fell prey to the politics of caste and opposed one other on caste lines. Kalineesan misguided the folks with falsehood and hatred.  The Europeans adapted divide and rule policy and ruled the state unleashing terror and fear.  Humanity and spiritual practices degenerated, chanting of sacred name of Hari stopped.  Rulers after rulers were wicked and under the influence of Kalian, dumbfounded people with the money power they wielded. At one period of time there were none to counter the influence of Kalian who ruled his land for over several thousand years by deceit and firmly established his influence and power throughout the vast land.
<br /><br />
Due to the influence of Kali illusion, when the Vedic Pundits of Srirangam temple were misbehaving with women inside the temple premises, vexed Lord Maha Vishnu decided to go away from there. In the meanwhile, Maharshi Shuka Brahma too requested Lord Narayana to go to Thiruvananthapuram to reform one of the Kings of Travancore to mend his ways who under the influence of Kalineesan ruled the land oppressing hapless clan called ‘Sandroars’ (highly poor people, oppressed and suppressed by the then rulers, belonging to over eighteen different castes like Nadars, Parathavar, Mukkuvar, Pulaiyar, Ezhavas, etc.). It firmed up the decision of Sri Maha Vishnu to leave that place. On way, he expediated the curses of 55 brahma rishis, standing as stone statues due to curse received from Lord Brahma, for having attempted to steal the birth-death account book privy to Lord Brahma. He also expediated the curse on a beautiful maiden called Ekkaala durkai, who remained a small mount on account of a curse received from Lord Shiva.  She wanted to take revenge on Lord Yama who killed her husband out of lust on her, and Lord Shiva advised her to wait for some time before Yama could be punished, but she defied his directive and hence got his curse.  While expediating the curse, Lord Vishnu restored her beauty and indicated the time frame when Lord Yama would get due punishment for the crime.   Similarly, the Lord appeared before another maiden who was in penance seeking punishment to Chitra Gupta the deputy to Lord Yama, who too killed her son out of lust on her. She wanted Chitra Gupta to be punished.  A Cow was also in penance seeking her son be reborn to her as her calf. Lord Vishnu revealed to both the time frame for the reward and then proceeded towards Thiruvananthapuram. 
<br /><br />
One of the Kings of Travancore under the influence of Kalineesan raised a big temple for Lord Mahavishnu (Ananta Padmanapa) in Thiruvananthapuram and performed rituals regularly. Unhappy over the rule of the King who oppressed and suppressed the hapless ‘Sandroars’ (the eighteen downtrodden folks like Nadars, Ezhavas, Baratava, Mukkuvar, Pulaiyar etc), infuriated Lord Maha Vishnu went to the ruler and warned him that if at all he wished his dynasty to continue the ruler of the land, then he should immediately desist from harassing or oppressing the hapless folks, who were the kins of Goddess Bhadra Kali born in the clan of Sandroars.  Lord further advised him to treat them with dignity like any other folks, lest ruin was certain to him and Kingdom which he had inherited would be lost. But the adamant King under the influence of evil Kali was determined not to change his style of function till he breathed last, no matter what may happen to him and openly displayed his hatred on Sandroars. Infuriated Lord Maha Vishnu challenged the King that though for the present he was proceeding to Tiruchendur, he would soon come back to unite the folks of all caste, make them love each other, and then destroy the Kingdom of the arrogant ruler.  The Lord left Thiruvananthapuram and went to Tiruchendur. 
<br /><br />
As the oppression and suppression of Sandroars continued in the rule of Kalian, the Celestial along with Goddess Parvathi met Lord Maha Vishnu and requested him to intervene and save the Sandroars from the oppressor. Realizing that the Kali maya (illusion of Kali) cannot be won over with weapons, Lord Maha Vishnu directed the Celestials, Rishi Munis, several other saints and Devaganas residing in divine abodes like Kailash, Vaikunda, Swarga log, Siva log, Yama log and other abodes to go and take birth in the clan of Sandroars.
<br /><br />
Next, when Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvathi along with Lord Maha Vishnu met the Celestial maidens who were sitting in penance in the forest, Lord Maha Vishnu not only assured them that he would marry them when he incarnated as Lord Vaikundar in Bhoologa, but also return their sons. He directed them to go to Bhoologa, take birth and wait for his incarnation.  Thereafter Lord Maha Vishnu also requested Goddess Mahalakshmi to go and remain inside the sea radiating golden rays like a huge flame of fire (Magara) since he was also destined to incarnate in Bhoologa to destroy Kalian. Heeding to his request Goddess Mahalakshmi too proceeded to Bhoologa and remained seated deep inside the Tiruchendur Sea radiating golden rays like flame of fire (Magara) around her. 
<br /><br />
As time passed, one day Lord Maha Vishnu suddenly recollected his earlier promise that he would incarnate in the form of a Pandaram to protect the sufferers under the influence of Kali and also remembered that his consort would be waiting inside the sea of Tiruchendur. In order to reconfirm whether appropriate time destroy evil Kali had arisen, he sought the advice of Veda Vyasa, who re-confirmed that the right time to take incarnation as Lord Vaikundar had already arrived.
<br /><br />
