One of the Devaganas had to take re-birth in Bhoologa as Sampoorana Devan alias Muthukutty (he is referred to only as Sampoorana Devan in Akilathirattu) to atone a sin accrued for showing lust and evil thoughts on the wife of another Devagana.  Once taken birth in Bhoologa, he married the same girl who had also taken rebirth, excessively enjoyed worldly pleasures and lust with her and fell seriously ill as destined and was brought to the seashore.  He got relieved of the curse since Lord Maha Vishnu had earlier promised that his curse would be removed when he (Lord) incarnate in Bhoologa. When Sampoorana Devan reached the seashore, Lord Vishnu too reached the seashore and relieved the curse of Sampoorana Devan as promised previously.
<br /><br />
<span style="font-size:16px;color:Maroon;">The incarnation of Lord Mahavishnu in Kali Yuga:</span> As prophesied in the Vedas, to destroy the influence of Kali along with the boons evil Kali carried, Lord Maha Vishnu descended on earth and entered into the sea of Tiruchendur where his consort Goddess Lakshmi was waiting for him inside the sea. He pushed the mind of Goddess Lakshmi into state of perturbation, aroused feelings in her and entered into her body only to come out himself in the form of a formless child in the universe on the 20th day of Tamil Month Masi in the year of Kollam, 1008 corresponding to Friday, the 1st March 1833 CE.  By the time the formless Lord reached the seashore, he disguised himself as Lord Vaikundar, the tenth incarnation of Lord Maha Vishnu. The sacred Pathi called ‘Avatharapathi’ lies in Tiruchendur seashore. This is one of the sacred Pathis in the Narayanaswami vazhi also called Ayya Vazhi.  
<br /><br />
