After reaching the seashore, Lord appeared in the form of a Pandaram (Mendicant), dressed up in ochre robe, braided hair, sacred white mark on forehead, Rudraksha mala (garland) around the neck, Rishi’s Wand and a Kamandal (a water-vessel of a religious mendicant) in hands and as if he was a Pandaram.  The celestial forces and Devaganas waiting for his arrival, prostrated at his feet and offered their obedience with lullabies and danced along the entire route in joy.
<br /><br />
