The saner advice of the elder fell in deaf ears of the ruler who failed to foresee the disaster awaiting him or the true spirits with which it was told. He lost his mental balance, got Lord Vaikundar arrested and imprisoned him in a place called Singarathoppu in Thiruvananthapuram. Though the ruler gave Lord Vaikundar alcohol mixed with poison to drink, it did not harm Lord Vaikundar in any manner. The ruler then brought a starving tiger in a cage and pushed Lord Vaikundar inside the cage hoping the tiger would eat him. The folks who were watching the cruel act cried aloud in helplessness, but the Lord counselled them ‘to remain calm since he had incarnated to end the evils of Kali. He claimed himself to be embodiment of Trinities, pervades everywhere including inside the animals, birds, reptiles and all other living beings, hence they need not worry about the tiger, which would definitely recognize divinity in him’.  
<br /><br />
