The starving tiger which was pushed inside the cage looked at the Lord for a while and instead of attacking him, it went near him, touched his feet as if prostrating, and sat by his side in silence. An impatient soldier prompted the tiger by pricking her with a long trident to attack the Lord. The tiger held the trident tightly under her body. In order to repick the tiger when the soldier attempted to pull back the trident with full force, the animal just released her grip over the Trident allowing it to fly back like an arrow and hit a Brahmin standing near the cage instantly causing death to the Brahmin. The ruler panicked because killing a Brahmin was greater sin than killing thousand cows, and he feared that his land has accrued sin. Everyone realized for certain that Lord Vaikundar indeed was divine incarnate, manifested to save the mankind from the evils of Kali.
<br /><br />
Though the ruler released Lord Vaikundar from prison, the Lord refused to immediately leave the place and continued to stay back in Thiruvananthapuram for some more days.  He informed the folks that he would leave the place on nineteenth day in the month Maasi and proceed to the eastern direction and those who wished to go along with him could proceed with him holding their spirits high like a bright lamp. The folks listened to him carefully and fell at his feet feeling their nightmare had ended. They got him seated on a cradle like palanquin and walked carrying him.  The Holy Akilathirattu viewed it as the beginning of the end of Kali along with the boons it carried since Lord Maha Vishnu, who was in disguise of a Pandaram had been maltreated.
<br /><br />
In order to strengthen the will power of the folks who followed him, Lord Vaikundar when reached Tamaraiyur Pathi, commenced a unique penance called Thuvayal Thavasu in which he enforced everyone to take ritual bath three times a day, wash their clothes daily, eat at noon with balanced food and offer prayers to him (Lord) in the language known to them. Besides they should also perform three-time prayers called Uga Padippu - both in the morning and evening and Uchchi Padippu in the noon (The Uga and Uchchi Padippu means Group prayer song sung in chorus to control the wavering mind and to beget the divine bliss).  With an intention to surrender at the feet of their Guru, who is ultimate (supreme being), they went to the northern entrance in Dwaragam Pathi called Vagai Pathi and penanced under the clear sky.   He enforced community dining where everyone irrespective of their caste and status- poor or rich- would sit and dine together in a common venue. When time passed, Lord Vaikundar appeared in the dream of one of the Sandroars to reveal that in a place called Mutta Pathi on the south-west, under the rule of Mukund (Lord Maha Vishnu), the victory flag of his empire has been established after destroying the evils. The greatness of the place cannot be explained in mere words. Those who stay there would   enormously benefit beyond their belief. When the folk conveyed his dream to everyone, all of them decided to move there. 
<br /><br />
