patimicaip patiyi nulle patintuvan tirunta rantae – Akilathirattu
</div>
<br /><br />
When Kalian began to proceed to Bhoologa with the boon he carried from Lord Shiva, Romarishi who was present in Deva Loga inquired from Lord Shiva when would Kali get destroyed. Lord Shiva replied that once the important divine mothers (not the seven maidens) got married in full purview of everyone in Bhoologa, count down for destruction of evil Kali will begin. When curious Romarishi, wanted to know who was likely to marry the divine mothers, Lord Shiva pronounced that when Lord Narayana incarnates as Lord Vaikundar embodied with the divine powers of us (Trinities -Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva) to destroy evil Kali and pick up good folks, he would marry the  divine mothers (except the seven maidens whom he had already married) and live  there happily with them.
<br /><br />
There in Bhoologa, in Tamaraiyur Pathi Lord Vaikundar continued to live happily in guise of human along with the seven maidens he had married earlier, intermittently displaying several divine plays. The place where the seven maidens lived is called Thottil Pathi. Prior to coming to Moolakundapathi after incarnated as Lord Vaikundar, as he walked towards south from the seashore, he established a Shiva ling in Moolakundapati, also known as Ambalapathi, offered worship and then hid it before proceeding further. He took an oath that he would come back again to worship the same Shiva Ling after performing several acts of divine plays, marry the seven maidens and completion of other duties. Because Lord Vaikundar had taken the oath thus, he decided to immediately go and settle in Moolakundapathi along with other folks who followed him. Lord Vaikundar publicly pronounced that ‘Moolakundapathi was a divine land, free of sins and those who visit there would be blessed with what they desire’. Accordingly, on reaching Moolakundapathi, he removed the sins of the folks which they had accrued out of misdeeds out of ignorance and lived there happily along with them. Every Tuesday, he appeared before the folks in his original form and prophesied the events forthcoming. 
<br /><br />
While living so in Moolakundapati, Lord Vaikundar realized that the time had come as foretold in the Agama to destroy Kali Yuga and therefore before going into the act of engaging Kali, he realized that he had to marry in public, enlightened and powerful Goddess Bhagavathi, Mandaikattal, Goddess Valli and Goddess Devasena.  He married all of them in Moolakundapathi Pathi also called Ambala Pathi   in full public view.   Accordingly, he married Goddess Bhagavathi (an aspect of Goddess Parvati) in the form of Lord Shiva, Mandaikattal (an aspect of Goddess Saraswathi) in the form of Lord Brahma and finally Goddess Valli and Goddess Devasena in the form of Lord Muruga.  He completed those tasks too in full public view.
<br /><br />
Listen Sandroars, in each of his incarnations in various Yugas, Lord Maha Vishnu had firmly established that the fleet of divines worshiped were not different from each other and though they may appear in different forms, they were all mirror images of Supreme Lord. By display of Visvaroopa darshan, he displayed the theory publicly. Only in order to deeply etch this fact into the minds of mankind and to ensure that they do not stand divided while worshiping different divines, he re-enacted several divine marriages. While Lord Maha Vishnu was happily spending his time with his followers, he told the Sandroars that he was delighted on the establishment of worship places (Pati) in their hometowns. They should spread the story of his ten incarnations, and the divine play enacted in which he measured the entire three worlds (Eternal space above, Earth and Underworld below earth) in three steps. Thereafter he visited the small shrines (Nizhal Thangals) built by the Sandroars, partook food, and continued to display divine acts of different kinds in nature.  The Lord took part in the feast along with his consorts in a place called Virunthetra Pathi also called as Thenthamaraaikkulam Pathi.  The folks eulogized Lord Maha Vishnu thus 'Like the dried crops which await the rains, we were waiting for your incarnation to save us from evil. Please forgive our wrong doings and bless us. We surrender at thine golden feet of thine as thee our savior and divine'. Meanwhile the Lord married in full view of the land another maiden Goddess Bhumadevi (Goddess of Earth), who had taken birth in the name of Goddess Poomadanthai and lived in a place called Soorangudi. While the Lord was returning, the place where the Celestial showered flowers on Lord Vaikundar and his consorts is called Poo Pathi. Thereafter the Lord happily settled in the Pathi along with others. 
<br /><br />
Finally, Lord Maha Vishnu who measured the soil in three steps proclaimed 'the atrocities committed by evil Kali in all the past seven Yugas would be scrutinized and judgment would be delivered based on the atrocities committed by him in the past. The boons enjoyed by Kalineesan would get destroyed, wrong doers sent to hell and the doors of hell would be locked to prevent their escape.  A new Dharma Yuga under the leadership of Dharmaraja would be established in Dwaraga Pathi where pious people would occupy the throne. There would be no inequality and everyone would live under one umbrella of rule’. He further promised that everything would happen in the glorious land of Dwaraga Pathi in full purview of the folks in the fourteen world and the folks could live there happily with their family. After retaining his incarnation in the Kaliyuga for over 18 years and 91 days, Lord Vaikundar realized that his duty was over and therefore decided to go back to Vaikunda. When the Pushpa Vimana (Aircraft) came to pick him up, he asked Maharishi Sathguru who accompanied the aircraft to wait for half an hour. He blessed his loving folks advising them to always remember the Lord in their mind and heart, remain united.  He called them near, gently rubbed their hands over his face and assured that he would in future appear in a new incarnation. He advised that they always remain cool and composed, help each other and live in peace and harmony. 
<br /><br />
At 12 noon on Monday, the 21st Vaikasi in the year Kollam 1026, (corresponding to 2nd June C.1851), Lord Maha Vishnu who had incarnated as Lord Vaikundar to protect and uplifting the life of oppressed Sandroars, ended his incarnation and returned back to Vaikunda.
<br /><br />
The Celestial from Deva Loga showered flower petals over Lord Vaikundar, while other divine forces sang hymns called Tirupattu (Thiru meaning venerable and Pattu meaning song) praising him.  Deva Loga dancers called Rambais (dancers) danced to the tunes of deafening drum beats played by the Sages and Rishis welcoming the Lord Vaikundar. They contended that Lord Vaikundar had indeed incarnated  in deference to the proclamations of Agama texts written several thousand years back. They placed a crown over his head, garlanded him and made him seated on a Lion faced Simhasan (Throne).  Seated on the throne of dharma, the Lord Vaikundar in the universe would be examining the state of affairs amongst the folks, by keeping away the falsehoods, and grace those who walk the path of dharmic practices as laid out in Veda agamas.
<br /><br />
<span style="font-size:16px;color:Maroon;">Lord Mahavishnu’s rule in Dharma Yuga:</span> As foretold in Veda Agama Akilathirattu ‘Lord Shiva, Goddess Parvathi, Lord Maha Vishnu, Goddess Lakshmi, Lord Brahma, Goddess Saraswathi and Vedic Maharishis are going to re-appear at the end of the present Yuga after which new Dharma Yuga would dawn.  As prophesied in the Vedas, Lord Maha Vishnu, would scrutinize all spheres-from sky to earth, and destroy Kalineesan ending Kali Yuga to pave way for the establishment of new Yuga, turning the universe into regenerated golden earth, true heaven, crystal clear sky, pure air, brighter moon, pious humans, new reptiles and other species of life.  As pre planed, on the directives of Lord Maha Vishnu the ocean would clean up the earth and then surrender to Lord. The evil would be destroyed with the birth of folks with good deeds and mind. The Lord would ensure that the overall situation in Dwaraga Pathi would turn splendid. 
<br /><br />
After the universe gets regenerated, the soul of evil Kroni would be paraded before the Lord when he would be grilled for his past acts. The Lord would question him 'Oh, evil, I bestowed several boons and ensured you take births in each of the past seven Yugas. I expected you to lead life of honor with dignity.  But you failed to meet my expectation and I had to incarnate in the form of a Pandaram to destroy the evils which were indulging in heinous crimes. I cured several diseases and ailments of the folks, sprinkling plain water and ensured that the folks with virtue get rewarded and vice punished. I banned the ritual of donations and other such kinds. I increased the determination of the folks. Contrary to what I did, you imprisoned and chained me to humiliate and torture me. Since I was in the form of a Pandaram I could not rebel against you.
<br /><br />
As a mendicant, I led simple life with alms taken from folks, at the same time curing their diseases and relieving stress just with plain water. Contrary to my service, what harm did I cause you?  You tortured me with acts of deceit. Have you forgotten the promise given that you would not torture or trouble any Pandaram or Mendicants and in the event the you broke the promise you would meet destruction with your entire family members?  Was it fair to harass me who was in the form of a Pandaram? Did you honor your promise, tell me oh, heinous evil, think whether you had done anything good in any one of the past seven births? If I had to reveal the extent of tortures and troubles faced by me, there would be no space to accommodate them even in all the seven worlds.
<br /><br />
'Oh, sinner, where are your forces, guards, palace, stooges and forces of Elephants? Where have they all gone?  You dug your own grave and met death by your own evil acts. You were responsible for creating your own destiny of destruction. By your heinous and evil act, in every one of your past births, you got killed ignominiously. In every one of your births, I too incarnated in some form to watch your acts and deeds, but you chose to torture and trouble those who chanted my name. You did not even show the least humanity expected and imprisoned and tortured them. That is why in one of your past births I cursed you that you would take birth by your own volition and get destroyed by your own evil acts.   
<br /><br />
'As destined, you were born in the name of Kalian and lived till now and met your end as destined due to your own evil acts. You are going to hell after surrendering the boons which I had bestowed besides surrendering the Chakrayutha (Hand held weapon wheel) given to you’.  Unable to reply to any of the charges leveled against him, Kalian would be sent to hell. After scrutinizing his evil acts, heinous crimes, inhuman acts, forgery, fraudulence and acts of deceit, he would get fair judgement from the Lord. He would be sent to hell and pushed to a place where both ‘fire’ and ‘death causing worms’ will eat him to end his life forever.
<br /><br />
Lord Maha Vishnu would continue to guard the same Universe which he has created.  As and when he decides to build new Dharma Yuga, he would blow a conch, the sound of which would reach all corners of the seven worlds when people with good virtues would begin to take birth followed by appearances of fresh trees, plants, vines, animals, reptiles and all chaste creatures.  Lord Maha Vishnu seated in the lion face studded golden throne embodied with thirty-two holy virtues, guarded on both sides by two golden skinned guards would again incarnate on earth to establish rule of Dharma and ensure people with good virtues to become rulers of the land.
<br /><br />
In the Kali Yuga, Lord Maha Vishnu appeared in the form of Pandara and settled in the southern end in the moth of Maasi in the year Kollam 1008 after taking birth in Tiruchendur. He enacted many divine plays and cured the dreaded diseases of people with simple water. He removed their sins, relieved their sufferings, bestowed several boons   for the welfare of mankind. He burnt the sins of many, married the seven maidens in full purview of the public and appeared in several divine forms to establish that all divines were one and the same. He ensured that the folks worshiped single divine, chanted the only sacred Nama mantra 'Ayya Siva Siva Siva, Siva Arahara Arahara'. With good teaching and preaching, he paved way for the folks to tread the path of Dharma. 
<br /><br />
As per a document available, it is believed that on hearing the news of Lord Vaikundar who was the incarnation of Lord Mahavishnu, Swami Vivekananda while on visit to Kanyakumari in December 1892 CE, went to Swamithoppu in Manavaipathi and   from then on, he reportedly began to wear a turban over his head. The followers of Lord Vaikundar consider the Holy text Akilathirattu Ammanai, as their Veda agama and believe in the principle of one God (Monotheism). Lord Vaikundar is affectionately called by the devotees as ‘AYYA’ because the Lord appeared and stayed with them in the form of a Pandaram (mendicant) in human form. Earlier known as Narayanaswamy Vazhi, it is now called as Ayya Vazhi. The temple of Ayya Vazhi exists in several parts of the world. Ayya Vazhi temple is also locally called as Narayanaswamy Kovil (Temple). His ideals are propagated through Pathis (place of God), which are congregational worship centers to propagate the teachings of Vaikundar.
<br /><br />
The Lord who incarnated in every one of the Yugas is going to destroy Kali yuga to pave way for the dawn of Dharma Yuga to be ruled by him.  Therefore, we too should tread the path of Dharma and walk in the way the Lord Ayya alias Vaikundar showed us to attain success in our life in the Dharma Yug.
<br /><br />
